#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""my-appCleaner -- uninstall a macOS app with everything it put on the machine.

`show <APP>` lists what an uninstall removes and why each item is there; `rm
<APP> go` removes it, to the owner's Trash; `intel` lists what has no
Apple-silicon code; `leftovers` lists Library files whose app is gone.
`my-appCleaner --help` says how to drive it.

One file, in this order:
  1. output, errors, config
  2. the system: commands, users, bundles, receipts, launchd, processes
  3. the plan: an <APP> -> every item, job and receipt, each with its reason
  4. verbs: show, rm, intel, leftovers
  5. cli, main, --run-tests
"""

